R-IX6 R-IX4 R-CV1 R-AD37 R-DI12 R-UP6 R-AP74 (slice 206e2b, D2): `tln upgrade --dry-run --offline` with a registry (config.toml, http://127.0.0.1:9), on the world of registry/ix6-update-offline (kept copies of the index reads, no GitHub page), and a kept `toolchains.json` of the registry (2 rows: 2026-10-12 and H = nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029, the roc: pin and the roc on PATH). The clock is 2026-10-20T12:00:00Z, so min-release-age (2 days) allows H.
`--offline` with a registry sends no request and uses the kept rows at any age (R-IX6, R-IX4). The compiler list of NightlyFlow.plan! is that file, not the GitHub cache (`talon/index/github/roc-lang/nightlies`, which this case does not have). So the list can be read: H is the newest compiler that the switch and the age allow, the nightly stays H with no note. Not `note: the compiler list could not be read; roc stays <H>` (that is the note of a list with no copy, Design Q489). The calls: `read_files` and `list_dirs` of the kept file, then the `pinned` query and write of the first sighting of the rows (R-CV6, as for a list from the file with a registry, slice 204); no `http_get`, no `http_send`.
The rest is the world of ix6-update-offline: json 2.1.0 and parser 1.2.0 from the kept copies, `pf: fixed: offline, no cached index`, `other: fixed: not in the registry index`, `index: cached at <oldest copy>` (the time of toolchains.json is not in it: a proposal, see the slice file, question Q1 of slice 206e2b), `resolved at <now>, N probes`. No download, no write except `projects.json`, `compat.db`.
